{"sp":["COMMITTEE CLERK","Chris Banks","David M. Carr","Sandra Ung","Hearing Testimony 4/16/26 (witness not identified)","SERGEANT MARINO","SERGEANT AT ARMS","Linda Lee","James F. Gennaro","Selvena N. Brooks-Powers","Oswald J. Feliz","Shaun Abreu","Crystal Hudson","Christopher Marte","Darlene Mealy","Mercedes Narcisse","Lincoln Restler","Nantasha M. Williams","Shirley Aldebol","Virginia Maloney","CHAIRPERSON JUSTIN SANCHEZ","Phil Wong","Frank Morano","INVOCATION DELIVERED BY","CITY CLERK","ALL","CLERK","Joann Ariola","DEPUTY LEADER BANKS","Gale A. Brewer","Carmen N. De La Rosa","Eric Dinowitz","Harvey D. Epstein","Simcha Felder","Shahana K. Hanif","Ty Hankerson","MAJORITY WHIP HANKS","Rita C. Joseph","Shekar Krishnan","Farah N. Louis"],"ro":["staff","council","written","administration","other"],"p":[[0,0,"Council Member Banks?"],[1,1,"(NO RESPONSE)"],[0,0,"Council Member Encarnación? COUNCIL MEMBER ENCARNACIÓN: I vote aye."],[0,0,"Council Member Carr."],[2,1,"Permission to explain my vote?"],[3,1,"Yes."],[2,1,"Thank you, Chair. Good morning, colleagues. You know, we're here today to consider a very important matter of the next appointment to Commissioner Investigations' role in our city. And I think that when we look at the appointments that come from any particular administration, there's an expectation, I think, from the Council that there'd be an alignment with the Mayor of the day on politics. There may even be close professional and political relationships with either\n\nthe Mayor or high-ranking members of the administration. But I think when it comes to the selection of the Commissioner of Investigation, it requires a different assessment from us as Council Members, one that ensures that the role has independence, and that there are not such close ties that, uh, potentially there is a future adversarial relationship, which may be required by an investigation with an administration, that it not be compromised in any way. And, and so I think that in the instance here, Ms. Shihata has a number of ties with the chief legal officer at City Hall, a person with whom there may be an adversarial relationship later down the line if an investigation were called upon into this administration. And I think it's important that the public be assured that the person who occupies this role and leads that investigation be sufficiently independent. Ms. Shihata is an incredibly well-credentialed person. I do not question her credentials, nor do I question her integrity as a\n\nperson or an attorney. I have confidence in her in that regard. However, I do feel that she should have made her several social media accounts available to the public, or at a minimum, the vetting unit of this Committee, so that we have an opportunity to examine her public utterances on policy matters, public matters. It may be that those accounts are benign or anodyne in terms of their content, but we do not know that at this point. And so given that that is the case, and my request to the Mayor's Office and to the appointee at the last hearing were not agreed to. And I will be voting no on this appointment. Thank you."],[0,0,"Council Member Banks?"],[1,1,"Aye."],[0,0,"With a vote of 8 in the affirmative, 1 in the negative, and no abstentions, the item has been adopted by the Committee. And Madam Chair, that is a full committee."],[3,1,"This committee is adjourned. (PAUSE)"],[3,1,"[GAVEL]\n\nWorld Wide Dictation certifies that the foregoing transcript is a true and accurate record of the proceedings. We further certify that there is no relation to any of the parties to this action by blood or marriage, and that there is no interest in the outcome of this matter. Date ____August 13, 2026_______________"],[4,2,"April 14, 2026"],[4,2,"To the Members of the City Council: We are writing to support the confirmation of Nadia Shihata to serve as the Commissioner of the Department of Investigation (DOI). We each served as the United States Attorney for the Eastern District of New Y ork (EDNY) during major periods of Ms. Shihata’s eleven years there. Ms. Shihata’s experience at one of the preeminent U.S. Attorney’s Offices in the country and unwavering integrity uniquely qualify her to serve New Y orkers once again at DOI. At the EDNY, Ms. Shihata was steadfast in her commitment to uphol ding and enforcing the rule of law fairly, without fear, favor, or bias. In her roles as Chief of the Organized Crime and Gangs Section, as well as Deputy Chief of the Office’s Public Integrity Section, Ms. Shihata led with courage and distinction . Whether she was leading investigations into a well -known R&B musician or the federal correction system, Ms. Shihata approached each case with the utmost seriousness and o bjectivity. She was an exemplary prosecutor, who focused on doing the right thing, holding wrongdoers accountable and keeping the public safe. Law enforcement relied upon her . Witnesses trusted her . And the community was safer because she was there. DOI plays a critical role in ensuring municipal transparency and accountability . Having worked closely with the DOI during our tenures as U.S. Attorney, we understand how important it is to have strong leadership at DOI . Over the course of her service to the public, Ms. Shihata has demonstrated that she has the experience, judgment and commitment to capably fill that role. At a time when public confidence in government institutions has been shaken, it is critical that highly qualified people with integrity fill key roles so that meaningful results are delivered for the people they serve. Ms. Shihata is imminently qualified with a proven record of effective service in the EDNY , and we have the utmost faith in her ability and character . We urge you to confirm Ms. Shihata to lead the DOI ."],[4,2,"Sincerely,\n\nLoretta E. Lynch Breon Peace U.S. Attorney, 1999 – 2001 and 2010 – 2015 U.S. Attorney, 2021 – 2025 U.S. Attorney General , 2015 – 2017"],[4,2,"/i255/1/2/3/4/5/i255/6/7/8/i255/9/10/9/11